{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "060T", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0009": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-finitely-presented-module}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:edc02ce56694407c8403a8e4832cf219c77e3c4adf5b683e818a7a9eea29def6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6f75ea09480b7529bca2656159934bfadfd3e494096ce35cb933c5eb46332c82", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0005>-module.\nAssume <MATH_0006> is finite and of finite presentation.\nThen <MATH_0007> is an <MATH_0008>-module of finite presentation\nif and only if <MATH_0009> is an <MATH_0010>-module of finite\npresentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1ec340b993feff2f978e19050bb0f26a16922860aa25922bc30f5ab7efc38ae4", "unit_id": "tag:0610:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "060T", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$V$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\to Y$", "MATH_0004": "$U = V \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\psi : U \\to V$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\psi_*(\\mathcal{F}|_U) = f_*\\mathcal{F}|_V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{descent-lemma-finite-finitely-presented-module}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:108ca53f30c8aaa9322482f73224d5f510d350695e7ca59118fede5df221bd7f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b468edcf020e6c7ca7cf6b4749fc709165e8b1e420e8cd38e5473bca81099a71", "source_text": "As <MATH_0001> is finite it is representable. Choose a scheme <MATH_0002> and a surjective\n<ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0003>. Then <MATH_0004> is a scheme with\na surjective <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism towards <MATH_0005> and a finite morphism\n<MATH_0006> (the base change of <MATH_0007>). Since\n<MATH_0008>\nthe result of the lemma follows immediately from the schemes version which\nis\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7db44d450684ffb534f7a2a6ad4b294d5b0d9d2a06fa64feb368880c391557eb", "unit_id": "tag:0610:proof"}
